---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Privacy Policy — pipper"
    description="How the pipper website and the Pipper Code desktop application collect, use, and protect your data."
    pageClass="legal-page"
>
    <article class="legal-shell w-full max-w-[46rem] mx-auto px-[clamp(1.25rem,4vw,2rem)] pt-12 md:pt-16 pb-20 flex flex-col gap-6 font-geist">
        <header class="legal-head flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h1 class="font-medium text-[clamp(1.8rem,4.5vw,3rem)] tracking-[-0.035em] leading-[1.1]">
                Privacy Policy
            </h1>
            <p class="text-[0.85rem] opacity-60">Last updated: August 9, 2026</p>
        </header>

        <div class="legal-body text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.7] min-w-0">
            <h2>1. Overview</h2>
            <p>
                This Privacy Policy explains what information the pipper website (pipper.dev) and
                the Pipper Code desktop application (together, the "Service") collect, how we use
                it, and the choices you have. We keep what we collect minimal.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Website Analytics</h2>
            <p>
                The website uses Vercel Web Analytics to collect aggregate, privacy-friendly usage
                statistics such as page views and referrer sites. This data is used to understand
                how visitors use the site and does not identify you personally.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Newsletter</h2>
            <p>
                If you subscribe to the Sandesh newsletter, we collect your email address and store
                it in Mailchimp, our email provider. We use it only to send you the newsletter you
                requested. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in every email, and we
                delete or retain your address only as long as you remain subscribed.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Accounts and Authentication</h2>
            <p>
                Sign-in and account features are powered by Clerk. When you sign in, Clerk processes
                your identity data (such as your name, email address, and avatar, depending on your
                identity provider) to authenticate you. We receive only limited account information
                needed for the Software to work. Your password is never handled by us.
            </p>

            <h2>5. The Desktop Application</h2>
            <p>
                The Software runs AI coding agents locally on your device. Your prompts, code, files,
                sessions, and agent activity stay on your machine. The Software does not transmit your
                source code, prompts, or agent outputs to us. Where the Software reaches out to your
                chosen AI agent providers, that traffic is between you and those providers and is
                governed by their privacy policies.
            </p>
            <p>
                The Website does check for available versions from our servers when you use the
                Download page, so we can present the latest release. That check does not include your
                personal data.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Community</h2>
            <p>
                If you join our Discord server or contribute to our public GitHub repository, any
                information you share there is governed by those platforms' own policies and is
                visible to members of those communities.
            </p>

            <h2>7. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
            <p>
                The website and Software may use local storage and cookies to keep you signed in and
                remember preferences. We do not use them for cross-site advertising trackers.
            </p>

            <h2>8. Data Sharing</h2>
            <p>
                We do not sell your personal data. We share data only with the service providers
                described above (Vercel, Clerk, Mailchimp) to operate the Software, and where required
                by law.
            </p>

            <h2>9. Retention and Your Rights</h2>
            <p>
                We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purposes above. Depending on your
                jurisdiction, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete your personal data; to
                opt out of marketing; and to request that we stop processing your data. To exercise
                these rights, contact us via the Discord server linked from the site.
            </p>

            <h2>10. Changes</h2>
            <p>
                We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by
                updating the "Last updated" date above.
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</Layout>

<style>
    :global(.legal-page) {
        background: #f0efed !important;
        color: #111111 !important;
    }
    .legal-shell h2 {
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        font-weight: 620;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        margin-top: 2rem;
    }
    .legal-shell p { color: rgb(17 17 17 / 0.78); }
</style>